    the following conditions:

    The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be
    included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

    THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.

cubiomes is otherwise used as a *reference* rather than adapted: the
known-answer vectors under tests/ are generated by running it at a pinned
commit (tools/vectors/), and its source is never vendored into this
repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
vanilla-mcdoc (MIT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The density function schema in lib/src/density_schema.inc and
lib/include/stratum/density/node_types.inc is generated by tools/mcdoc-sync
from the mcdoc schema definitions published by SpyglassMC at
https://github.com/SpyglassMC/vanilla-mcdoc, under the MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2022 SpyglassMC.

The schema is fetched at a pinned commit and never vendored: this
repository ships the tool and the generated tables, not the upstream
source tree. SPEC section 11 requires the schema be derived rather than
hand-written, so that a field name cannot drift from what the format
actually specifies.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
xoroshiro128++ (public domain)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

lib/include/stratum/rng/xoroshiro128.hpp reimplements the xoroshiro128++
generator by David Blackman and Sebastiano Vigna, published at
https://prng.di.unimi.it/xoroshiro128plusplus.c and dedicated to the public
domain. No attribution is required; it is recorded here because this
repository records every outside reference it builds on.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
zlib (linked dependency)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Region files store chunks deflated, so the engine links zlib
(https://zlib.net/), by Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler, under the zlib
license. It is used as a dependency, not vendored: a system zlib is
preferred, and one is fetched and built only when the platform has none.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
fdlibm (SunPro)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

lib/src/fdlibm_log.cpp is adapted from fdlibm 5.3, file e_log.c
(version 1.3, 95/01/18), obtained from https://www.netlib.org/fdlibm/.
It carries the upstream notice in its file header, reproduced here:

    ====================================================
    Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved.

    Developed at SunSoft, a Sun Microsystems, Inc. business.
    Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this
    software is freely granted, provided that this notice
    is preserved.
    ====================================================

This notice must be preserved in any distribution of that file;
tools/lint/check-determinism.sh fails the build if it is removed.

The reason for vendoring rather than calling the platform's libm is
recorded in SPEC section 11: Java's StrictMath is fdlibm, and a host libm
differs from it by up to one unit in the last place, which breaks Tier-A
parity. This code was taken from netlib, NOT from OpenJDK's StrictMath,
which is GPL+CE and incompatible with this repository's license.
